{"title":"Parabola","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>parabola</b> is a type of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Conic_section\" title=\"Conic section\">conic section</a>.  A parabola is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Locus\" title=\"Locus\">locus</a> of points that are equidistant from a point (the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Focus\" title=\"Focus\">focus</a>) and a line (the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Directrix\" title=\"Directrix\">directrix</a>). \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Parabola_Equations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Parabola Equations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Graphing_Parabolas\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Graphing Parabolas</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Parabola_Equations\">Parabola Equations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Parabola Equations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:5px;float:right;margin:10px;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6bcdb93e775ec964d737dbd3d1ba4f5dfdc23a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(100); // Square canvas Label f;  f.p = fontsize(6);   // Axes: from -8 to 8 with tick steps of 2 xaxis(-8, 8, Ticks(f, 2.0));  yaxis(-8, 8, Ticks(f, 2.0));   // Define the function real f(real x) { return x^2; }  // Draw from x = -3 to x = 3 (main visible part of the parabola) draw(graph(f, -3, 3), blue+linewidth(1)); [/asy]\" width=\"165\" height=\"168\" />\t\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"magnify\" style=\"float: right;\">\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Enlarge.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/15px-Enlarge.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"15\" height=\"9\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/23px-Enlarge.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/30px-Enlarge.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div> Graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef862bdd16c2d5356e11735b8c766c402f5e10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>There are several \"standard\" ways to write the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> of a parabola. The first is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a> form: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec7caaaa99ef059f75508e38eefb48f129b0545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = a{x}^2+b{x}+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> where a, b, and c are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constants</a>. This is useful for manipulating the polynomial. \n</p><p>The second is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\"> completed square</a> form, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618d32a3bc4a098382619ad35e4edb70f391c44a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a(x-h)^2+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" /> where a, h, and k are constants and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertex</a> is (h,k). This is very useful for graphing the quadratic because the vertex and stretching factor are immediately before you. \n</p><p>The third way is the conic section form, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e46cf48df70a1778812d42559b4c19870dc0ee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=4px$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d46626ea46ddd29f5fa371d5f9497decd84536e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=4py$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> where the p is a constant, and is the distance from the focus to the vertex.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Graphing_Parabolas\">Graphing Parabolas</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Graphing Parabolas\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the completed square form, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a055bcdae40ffbf346cfe2b4ad9db8a0ff63cde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - k = a(x - h)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae693ea0d4d11b1a301339140a617adb2e8f565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - h = a(y - k)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"19\" />, the vertex of the graph is at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907d3475bdca1d395b0a65a63ccda4cf912b6081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(h, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />. The graph appears vertically if the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> term is squared, and horizontal if the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> term is squared. The graph will be oriented (opens up) upwards/right if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, and will be downwards/left if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is negative.\nHere are the graphs of a few parabolas:\n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/dda1c136b9dc5d5fb5a7dbf5b6ae246bc68b3c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2-14x+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef05cddb62e9f4a3185f556405ec61a88c1c91b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(300);  Label f;  f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(-9,9,Ticks(f, 1.0));  yaxis(-9,9,Ticks(f, 1.0));  real f(real x)  {  return 3x^2-14x+8;  }  draw(graph(f,(7+2*sqrt(13))/3,(7-2*sqrt(13))/3),red+linewidth(1)); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"502\" /></center>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceaad52176efe9df90583ed9f5c7d51661fe5ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^2+2x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is negative)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d9ba587243d9b1155bf2e547df7685ebabd990.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(300);  Label f;  f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(-8,8,Ticks(f, 2.0));  yaxis(-8,8,Ticks(f, 2.0));  real f(real x)  {  return -x^2+2x+2;  }  draw(graph(f,1-sqrt(11),1+sqrt(11)),green+linewidth(1)); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"502\" /></center>\n<p><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Description\">Video Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Description\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Res-cddhRLw?si=a2XGd_hkEArrwOVG\">https://youtu.be/Res-cddhRLw?si=a2XGd_hkEArrwOVG</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ol><li>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">parabola</a> with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba697e110eb547ec3222ea358ed4c1060ac37887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> passes through the points (2,3) and (4,3).  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?<br /><br /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5bdc5211a6ebb6b5fe3afc944497d6855394fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 2\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 5\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 7\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 10\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"18\" /><div style=\"text-align:right;\">(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">2006 AMC 10A, Problem 8</a>)</div></li></ol>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ol><li>Suppose that a parabola has vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb999f6b1518b2af1bbf4299cfa9044809ca889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4},-\\frac{9}{8}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" /> and equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84cea4f7bfc5284747e737af0d1a25e64afdd47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer.  The minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9ba2bd66bae47ebdda2382ef31dbb4c241e0db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. <div style=\"text-align:right;\">(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">2011 AIME I, Problem 6</a>)</div></li></ol>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ol><li>Find the area of the largest triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> [and prove this is the maximum] whose interior is entirely within the region bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d124a5b59f8b7cad1e65bdd87440de6accd23a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sqrt{3}x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350701b76d7969daa75f981eab7f96c58cca74d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3x^2-12x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ol>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hyperbola\" title=\"Hyperbola\">Hyperbola</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">Circle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse\" title=\"Ellipse\">Ellipse</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018102558\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\